SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1776025044
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,4,F
OL,5, The 1986 Chinook helicopter crash off
OL,6, Shetland in which 45 people died was
OL,7, caused by a failure of the aircraft's
OL,8, gear system, says an official riport.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe report of the Department of
OL,11,FTransport's Air Accident Investigation
OL,12,FBranch says the failure was brought
OL,13,Fabout by a new design of bolted joint.
OL,15,FNeither the authorities nor the makers,
OL,16,FBoeing, explored the joint's working
OL,17,Fcharacteristics enough to expose its
OL,18,F"inherent weakness", says the report.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FIt calls for all modifications to vital
OL,21,Fparts to be "adequately scrutinised".
OL,22,F
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49607
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1776025044
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,4,F
OL,5, Manufacturers and air authorities were
OL,6, wrong to assume that a new joint would
OL,7, behave like the old one, says a report
OL,8, on the 1986 Chinook helicopter crash.
OL,10,FIt says the previous processes of
OL,11,Fapproval used by the Federal Aviation
OL,12,FAdministratign and the Civil Aviation
OL,13,FAuthority were inadequate for such
OL,14,Fa modified vital component.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FIt concluded that better monitoring
OL,17,Fmight have given indications which
OL,18,Fcould have prevented the accident.
OL,20,FThe report also recommended a review
OL,21,Fof the certification process.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49608
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1776025044
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,4,F
OL,5, Publication of the original AAIB report
OL,6, into the 1986 Chinook helicopter crash
OL,7, was delayed because the makers, Boeing,
OL,8, asked for a review of the report.
OL,10,FThe Department of Transport's Review
OL,11,FBoard carried out the review and agreed
OL,12,Fwith the AAIB's findings.
OL,14,FBut Boeing was concerned that the
OL,15,FReview Board report contained a
OL,16,F"serious miscarriage of justice" and
OL,17,Fthis further delayed its publication.
OL,19,FThe DoT said today that there was no
OL,20,Fground for suspecting that there had
OL,21,Fbeen a miscarriage of justice.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49609
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1776025044
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Boeing has accepted the official
OL,6, report's view of the cause of the 1986
OL,7, Chinook helicopter crash.
OL,9,FThe plane manufacturer also accepted
OL,10,Fthe report's conclusion that test
OL,11,Fprocedures were not adequate.
OL,13,FBut Boeing pointed out that the
OL,14,Fmodification on the crashed helicopter
OL,15,Fhad not been made properly.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FBoeing added that a senior engineer
OL,18,Fwith the operating company had said
OL,19,Fthat something was wrong two months
OL,20,Fbefore the accident, but his
OL,21,Frecommendations were not followed.
OL,22,F
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49610
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1776025044
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G10/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Transport Secretary has said an
OL,6, "appalling tragedy" like the King's
OL,7, Cross fire must never happen again.
OL,9,FMr Paul Channon said London Underground
OL,10,Fchiefs had reacted "seriously and
OL,11,Fresponsibly" to criticisms levelled at
OL,12,Fthem after the fire in November 1987.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FHe was opening a Commons debate on
OL,15,Fthe report on the fire by Mr Desmond
OL,16,FFennell, QC, which criticised London
OL,17,FUnderground's approach to safety.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FLabour spokesman Mr John Prescott said
OL,20,Fspending cuts on the underground were a
OL,21,Fmajor factor in the King's Cross fire.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1776025044
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G11/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, An investigation has been ordered after
OL,6, criticism of the way the emergency
OL,7, services handled the King's Cross fire.
OL,9,FTransport Secretary Mr Paul Channon
OL,10,Fordered the inquiry after receiving
OL,11,Fa letter from former London Regional
OL,12,FTransport chairman Sir Keith Bright.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FSir Keith said Underground managers
OL,15,Fhad identified "gaps" in the emergency
OL,16,Fservices' action in the official report
OL,17,Fon the fire by Mr Desmond Fennell, QC.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FThese included fire officers' failure
OL,20,Fto evacuate the station and to tackle
OL,21,Fthe fire with fire extinguishers.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49612
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1776025044
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G12/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, The Fennell report on the King's Cross
OL,6, fire commended the individuals involved
OL,7, but criticised many of the systems.
OL,9,FLondon Underground staff were untrained
OL,10,Ffor such an emergency, despite being
OL,11,Ftold to deal with fires themselves.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FCommunications equipment was faulty
OL,14,For unused; the control room was not
OL,15,Fstaffed at the time of the disaster
OL,16,Fand an inexperienced inspector took
OL,17,F12 minutes to inform his supervisor.
OL,19,FThere was no evacuation plan and no
OL,20,Fsupervisory staff on hand to help
OL,21,Fpolice unfamiliar with the station.
OL,22,F
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49613
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1776025044
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G13/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, Fennell report recommendations include:
OL,7,S(FRegular cleaning, inspection and
OL,8,Freplacement of escalators.
OL,9,F
OL,10,S(FStaff training, clearly-marked fire-
OL,11,Ffighting equipment, closer Fire Brigade
OL,12,Flinks, panic bars for locked gates,
OL,13,Fimproved communications epuipment.
OL,14,C
OL,15,S(FLRT to establish an effective safety
OL,16,Fmonitoring system; London Underground
OL,17,Fto have a director responsible for
OL,18,Fsafety with access to the chairman.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FBoth bodies are to report on their
OL,21,Fprogress in implementing the above
OL,22,Fto the Transport Secretary.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
